{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. Each lottery has two outcomes, so the threshold for an outcome to be considered 'probable' is 1 divided by 2, i.e., 50%. In Lottery A, the outcomes are -3000 Euros (0.2%) and 0 Euros (99.8%). In Lottery B, the outcomes are -6000 Euros (0.1%) and 0 Euros (99.9%). Since both non-zero outcomes (0.2% and 0.1%) are far below the 50% threshold, only the 0 Euro outcome in each lottery qualifies as 'probable'. The average of the probable outcomes is therefore 0 for both lotteries. Thus, according to the decision reason, the individual should be indifferent between A and B.",
